    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nGlebe House at Aglish is a beautifully presented and positioned period residence. Dating from approx. 1820, set amidst approx. 4.02 hectares (9.93 acres) of paddocks and stunning grounds, featuring an original walled garden, mature native trees, and tremendous privacy. \nExtending to approximately 232 sq. m. (2,500 sq. ft.) Glebe House offers a sense of calm, peace, and grace, and is in wonderful condition throughout. The location is convenient to Terryglass, Lough Derg (10 kms), Nenagh (25 kms) & Limerick (65 kms). \nThis beautiful house stands two storeys over garden level and retains a wealth of original character, with elegant reception rooms, traditional fireplaces, modern heating systems, a perfectly preserved lower ground floor with a warm kitchen complete with Aga. There is also a converted three bedroomed Coach House to the rear that can generate an income, accommodate family and friends, or indeed provide space to conduct a business from home. \nThe rooms throughout both are elegantly appointed, with a neutral decor palette, and from the main house there are beautiful views of gardens. Modern bathrooms, new boilers & wood burning stoves have been installed, and overall, this is a very manageable and comfortable country home. \nWithin the main house accommodation comprises four reception rooms, a kitchen, three bathrooms, four bedrooms and plenty of storage. The Coach House provides another three bedrooms, two bathrooms, a sitting room, and a dining room. \nThe landscaped grounds include manicured lawns, mature trees, and a charming walled garden with an orchard. An attractive tiled courtyard connects the house and coach house and there are useful out buildings providing plenty of storage for garden equipment, logs, a boat, etc. \nGlebe House at Aglish enjoys a peaceful rural setting in North County Tipperary, within easy reach of the market towns of Borrisokane, Roscrea, Birr, and Nenagh, as well being convenient to Limerick. \nThe surrounding countryside is renowned for its scenic beauty, while the nearby shores of Lough Derg offer an excellent range of leisure and recreational pursuits, including boating, fishing, walking, and water sports. The picturesque lakeside villages of Terryglass and Portumna are within easy reach, with Portumna also providing a forest park, golf course, and a wide range of amenities.\nThere are four Golf courses within twenty minutes' drive of the house. Shannon Airport is approximately 85 km away, a journey of about 1 hour by car, making both domestic and international travel readily accessible. Viewing so recommended, please call Julie Fogarty, Sherry FitzGerald Fogarty 0505 21192."
      },
      {
